To my knowledge, the proposed method is novel. Furthermore, the paper is technically sound.

The paper is generally clear, and I would just like to point a few typos and imprecisions:

-"Stochastic simulations are fundamental to many scientific fields (Ripley, 2009), especially epidemic modeling". As it is phrased, it seems to suggest that stochastic stimulations are more important in epidemiology than in other scientific fields (which is arguably not true), whereas the authors probably wanted to write that stochastic simulations are important in epidemiology;

-"Noted if the spatial dependency", instead "Note that if the spatial dependency";

-"is replaced to Convolutional LSTM layer", instead "is replaced by a Convolutional LSTM layer";

-"are independent with each other", instead "are independent of each other";

-probably better to drop the word "acquiring" in "as acquiring points that are informative individually are not necessarily informative jointly";

-in "The total number of dimension", it should be "dimensions". There are a few other instances of "dimension" where this should also be corrected;

-"Figure 3 right visualize the STNP predictions", instead "Figure 3 right shows the STNP predictions";

-Figure 5, yellow dots and red stars need to be larger for easier visualisation.
